coder › Done. Implemented `compareSemver` in `src/semver.ts` and the test suite in `src/semver.test.ts`, committed as `883969f` on `work/main`.

**Implementation notes** (a couple of small decisions beyond the letter of the spec, all behavior-preserving):
- Validation, core/prerelease extraction, and build-metadata dropping all happen through the single anchored regex — the captures yield major/minor/patch and prerelease directly, so "cut at `+`, then split at `-`" never has to be done by hand and can't disagree with what was validated. Build metadata (capture 5) is simply never read.
- Both inputs are fully validated up front (a first, b second) before any comparison, so an invalid `b` never throws when `a` is invalid — matching "validate a first."

**Tests** cover every item listed plus a few: large-number ordering (`10.0.0 > 9.0.0`, `1.0.10 > 1.0.9`), build metadata not affecting core comparison, and extra invalid cases (`v1.0.0`, `1.0.0.0`, `1.0.0-01`). Each invalid value is asserted to throw naming the offending string in both argument positions, and there's a check that `a` is validated before `b`.

